    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`jit-kernel-unit-test-4-gpu-b200` fails on every PR that runs it since #44418 merged:\n\n```\nFAILED registered/kernels/ops/diffusion/test_nvfp4_scaled_mm.py::test_flux2_swizzled_scale_checkpoint_flashinfer_trtllm_matches_cudnn - AssertionError: assert False\n```\n\n#44418 moved the swizzled-to-row-major conversion for swizzled NVFP4 checkpoints into the `weight_scale` loader, and marks the parameter as holding row-major scales whenever a loader is present. The test's `_build_layer` passes a no-op loader and copies the checkpoint scales straight into the parameter, so the swizzled bytes reach a layer that now expects row-major ones. The serving path is fine; the test bypasses the step that moved.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`_build_layer` passes a loader that copies, and loads `weight_scale` through the parameter's own `weight_loader`, the way a checkpoint load does. No product code changes.\n\n## Test plan\n\nOn a Blackwell GPU (GB300):\n- `test_nvfp4_scaled_mm.py` on main: 1 failed, 12 passed. With this change: 13 passed.\n- Bisect over the 78 commits since the test last passed locates #44418 (`09b7383624`) as the first failing commit.\n- With this change applied before #44418 (`2f5407da28`): 13 passed, so the test does not depend on the new code path.\n- Negative control: removing the loader's swizzled-to-row-major conversion makes the fixed test fail again.\n- `black`, `isort`, `ruff check --select=F401,F821,F823,UP037` clean on the changed file.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38838823984](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38838823984)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38838823626](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38838823626)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #38838823986](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38838823986)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
